The '''Appenzell Alps''' ({{langx|de|Appenzeller Alpen}}) are a [[mountain range]] in [[Switzerland]] on the northern edge of the [[Alps]]. They extend into the [[Cantons of Switzerland|cantons]] of [[Appenzell Ausserrhoden]], [[Appenzell Innerrhoden]] and [[St. Gallen (canton)|St. Gallen]] (with lower summits occurring also in the cantons of [[Thurgau]] and [[canton of Zurich|Zurich]]){{efn|In the northwest and north of the Appenzell Alps, there are several proposed border demarcations between them and the [[Appenzell]] and [[Toggenburg]] regions and the Swiss [[Prealps]]: The border drawn in the [[Swiss Alpine Club]] guidebook runs along a line from [[Uznach]] over the [[Ricken Pass]] to [[Wattwil]]. From there, it ascends the Toggenburg region to [[Nesslau]] and over the Chräzeren Pass near [[Schwägalp Pass|Schwägalp]] to [[Urnäsch]]. From there, the border runs directly east to Appenzell and further north past the Fähnern summit into the [[Alpine Rhine Valley]]. However, peaks still exist north of this border, reaching an altitude of {{convert|1528|m}} at the [[Hochalp]]. Depending on the perspective, one or more of these northern peaks may therefore still be considered part of the Appenzell Alps.}} and are bordered by the [[Schwyz Alps]] to the southwest, the [[Glarus Alps]] to the south, and the [[Rätikon]] to the south-east, and cover an area of about {{cvt|1800|km2}}.<ref>{{Cite book |last=Höhne |first=Ernst |title=Die Alpen zwischen Matterhorn und Bodensee |publisher=[[Droemer Knaur]] |year=1987 |isbn=978-3-426-26223-8 |series=Knaurs Lexikon für Bergfreunde / Ernst Höhne |location=München |pages=29 |language=de |trans-title=The Alps between the Matterhorn and Lake Constance}}</ref> The highest summit is the [[Säntis]], with an [[elevation]] of {{cvt|2502|m}}.

==Sub-ranges==
The range is split up into six sub-ranges:
* '''[[Alpstein]]'''
** Central group, highest summit: Altmann, {{cvt|2435|m|ft|disp=x| / }}
** Northern group, highest summit: Säntis, {{cvt|2502|m|ft|disp=x| / }}
** Southern group, highest summit: Roslen- or Saxerfirst, {{cvt|2151|m|ft|disp=x| / }}
* '''{{ill|Alvier group|de|Alviergruppe}}''', highest summit: Gamsberg, {{cvt|2385|m|ft|disp=x| / }}
* '''[[Churfirsten]]''', highest summit: Hinterrugg, {{cvt|2306|m|ft|disp=x| / }}
* '''Speer - Mattstock''', highest summit: Speer, {{cvt|1950|m|ft|disp=x| / }}

